  {
    "id": "anno-lower_p241_left-04",
    "type": "Annotation",
    "body": [
      {
        "purpose": "transcribing",
        "value": "一二三番小隊　百四十四人〔小隊四十人ツヽ隊長敎頭司令官／小長迄役司組込四十八人ツヽ二三番同断〕"
      },
      {
        "purpose": "modern_jp_reading",
        "value": "一・二・三番小隊 144人〔小隊四十人ずつ、隊長・教頭・司令官・小長まで役司組込四十八人ずつ、二・三番同断〕"
      },
      {
        "purpose": "english_translation",
        "value": "[Shizuku] Nos. 1, 2 and 3 platoons: 144 men. The long warichu below the figure is read right sub-column first, then left: 小隊四十人ツヽ、隊長敎頭司令官 / 小長迄役司組込四十八人ツヽ、二三番同断 — 'forty men to a platoon; with the officers, from company commander, drill-master and commanding officer down to the junior leader, counted in, forty-eight each; Nos. 2 and 3 the same.' The arithmetic closes: three platoons at forty-eight each is the 144 printed above, and the forty men without officers gives 120 rank and file."
      },
      {
        "purpose": "identifying",
        "value": "志筑小隊"
      }
    ],
