    "body": [
      {
        "purpose": "transcribing",
        "value": "新渡戸大參事〔平常／澄〕"
      },
      {
        "purpose": "modern_jp_reading",
        "value": "新渡戸大参事〔平常／澄〕"
      },
      {
        "purpose": "english_translation",
        "value": "[Shichinohe] Senior councillor: Nitobe. The surname is followed by the office written out again, 新渡戸大參事, which is how the entries in this stretch of fascicle 9 set a named officer — the facing pages print 馬場權大參事, 金井少參事 and 西田少參事 the same way. Below it stands a three-glyph warichu in reduced type: 平常 in the right sub-column and 澄 in the left. Comparable entries put the officer's given name in that slot, but how these three glyphs divide between a clan name, a given name and an editorial note cannot be settled from this leaf, and no reading is offered here."
      },
      {
        "purpose": "identifying",
        "value": "七戸大參事新渡戸"
      }
